# --- Required: a model, plus credentials for it ---
# Every LLM stage follows HANDYMAN_MODEL — any pydantic-ai model string works.
# The default runs Claude on AWS Bedrock via standard AWS credential
# resolution (AWS_PROFILE / env keys / instance role):
HANDYMAN_MODEL=bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5
# AWS_PROFILE=your-bedrock-profile
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# A Bedrock application-inference-profile ARN also works as the model id —
# useful for per-project cost attribution:
# HANDYMAN_MODEL=bedrock:arn:aws:bedrock:REGION:ACCOUNT:application-inference-profile/ID

# No AWS? Either single-key alternative behaves identically:
# HANDYMAN_MODEL=anthropic:claude-sonnet-5    with  ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# HANDYMAN_MODEL=openai:gpt-5                 with  OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# The eval gate's case model (the "consumer" whose tool selection is being
# tested). Defaults to haiku-tier on Bedrock/Anthropic — a weaker model is a
# stricter test of the descriptions, at a third of the price. Providers
# without a weak-tier mapping (OpenAI) reuse the pipeline model instead.
# HANDYMAN_EVAL_MODEL=bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0

# --- Recommended ---
# api.weather.gov asks clients to identify themselves via User-Agent and may
# throttle anonymous traffic. Any app name + contact works. The design stage
# names this variable after the server it generates — the committed server
# reads WEATHER_GOV_USER_AGENT; after a regeneration, check the generated
# README's configuration table.
WEATHER_GOV_USER_AGENT="handyman-demo (you@example.com)"

# Where "home" is for the weather demo task (default: Seattle).
HOME_LAT=47.6062
HOME_LON=-122.3321

# --- Optional ---
# Stream pipeline + agent traces to Logfire (https://logfire.pydantic.dev).
# Absent, tracing is a local no-op.
# LOGFIRE_TOKEN=

# Only needed for the `arcade deploy` flourish (publishing a generated server
# to Arcade Cloud). Not used by the local demo path.
# ARCADE_API_KEY=arc_...
